From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: ticker for new notifications on the lock screen
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A one-line ticker at the top of the Sable locked glance (Sable 2.0
plan): when a notification the lock screen shows arrives, or alerts
again, while the lock screen is up and the screen is on, one line
scrolls across for 10 seconds: "WhatsApp: Maya · See you at 6". The
title and text show only when the lock screen may show that
notification's content (no public mode with content hidden, no
redaction); otherwise it reads "WhatsApp: New notification". Silent,
ambient, ongoing and group summary notifications get no ticker, nor do
updates that only alert once. The line goes when its notification is
removed, on unlock and while dozing; Lock screen size scales it. The
rules are pure Java (SableLockGlance.tickerWorthy and tickerLine, unit
tested).
